[h1]OpenZone Factions[/h1]
The faction system of the OpenZone series: factions and organisations, membership, roles and posts, ranks, rosters, leadership, permadeath, spawn loadouts, and the admin surface for all of it. A companion of OpenZone Core, not a part of it: Core only asks who a player belongs to, this mod answers. Part of the OpenZone series, made for the whole Ukrainian DayZ community.

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Membership, ranks and posts kept in the database of the OpenZone bridge, so they survive character death and server wipes.
[*]Leadership and roles: who leads, who may invite and promote, what a post allows.
[*]Permadeath: a dead character's faction life is closed the way the server's rules say.
[*]Spawn loadouts: presets per faction and rank, walked as a ladder (organisation and rank, organisation, base faction and rank, base faction), with modifiers by post or trait; an empty ladder leaves the mission's own dressing in place.
[*]A Discord mirror: the roster and its changes reflected into the guild. Discord itself is optional and can be switched off; the bridge is not.
[*]The FACTIONS admin section: membership and roles managed in game.
[/list]
[b]Requires[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798432022]OpenZone Core[/url], and the OpenZone bridge running on the server ([url=https://github.com/covalschi/openzone-bridge]github.com/covalschi/openzone-bridge[/url]). There is no "factions without the bridge" configuration.
[b]Companions[/b] [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798436427]OpenZone Factions PDA[/url] (the Faction tab in the PDA), [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3798436511]OpenZone Factions VPP[/url] (the FACTIONS pane in the admin tab).
[b]Source code[/b] [url=https://github.com/covalschi/openzone-factions]github.com/covalschi/openzone-factions[/url]

[b]Licence, repacking, selling[/b]
You may repack this mod into your server's own pack, keeping the attribution and the same licence. You may not sell it, sublicense it or include it in any paid bundle. Running it on a server that accepts donations, sells cosmetics or priority queue slots is fine. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with the additional permission in NOTICE.

